  "title": "YouTube Data API: Favorite & Like Activities Removed",
  "summary": "The `favorite` and `like` activity types, along with their corresponding properties in `ActivityContentDetails`, have been removed from the API. Developers relying on these fields will encounter breaking changes. Conversely, the `subscription` activity type and its details are no longer deprecated.",
  "details": "This update introduces breaking changes for applications consuming YouTube activity feeds. The `favorite` and `like` properties are no longer available within the `schemas.ActivityContentDetails` object. Consequently, the `ActivityContentDetailsFavorite` and `ActivityContentDetailsLike` schemas, which described these activity types, have also been removed entirely. Developers should update their code to no longer expect these fields or schemas.\n\nAdditionally, the `ActivitySnippet.properties.type` enum has been restructured, removing `like` and `favorite` as valid activity types. On a positive note, the `subscription` property within `ActivityContentDetails` and the `ActivityContentDetailsSubscription` schema are no longer marked as deprecated, indicating continued support for this activity type. Several descriptions for various enum values and parameters have also been clarified.",
